  },
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>All resistances in figure are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math> each. The value of current &#39;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi></math>&#39; is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math>&nbsp;is _____ .</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0161_f3c7af9d5470.png\" style=\"width: 350px; height: 217px;\" /></p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "8",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0161_f2d1a57c0d77.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 215px;\" /></p><p>Each pair on the right side of the circuit is in parallel connection, hence it can be replaced by a resistance of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;as shown.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0161_dde7bdf4ca63.png\" style=\"width: 310px; height: 148px;\" /></p><p>Now,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;in each branch on the right side is in series, hence combined resistance value will be,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>r</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>. Upper branch having resistance&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>r</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;is in parallel with another&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>r</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>, hence it can be written as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>r</mi></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0161_c3a987a1218b.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 176px;\" /></p><p>Further, simplified circuit will have net resistance of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>7</mn><mi>r</mi></mrow><mn>8</mn></mfrac></math>.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0161_bb089c9d2c50.png\" style=\"width: 220px; height: 192px;\" /></p><p>Therefore,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>eq</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>7</mn><mi>r</mi></mrow><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>7</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>15</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math></p><p>Now, current&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>15</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math></p><p>Hence, value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></math>.</p>"
  }
}